# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: dxf-file-angle-units — the DXF codec copies file angles (degrees) into entget data (radians) unconverted
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-dxf-file-angle-units
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

A DXF file stores most entity angles in DEGREES (ARC 50/51, TEXT / MTEXT /
ATTRIB / ATTDEF / INSERT / SHAPE 50, DIMENSION 53, ...); AutoLISP's entget
reports them in RADIANS. clautolisp's DXF codec
(=clautolisp/drawing/source/dxf.lisp=) has no degrees <-> radians conversion
at all, on read or on write, so:

- a drawing written by AutoCAD / BricsCAD and opened in clautolisp shows an
  ARC of 0..90 degrees as =(50 . 0.0) (51 . 90.0)= in entget -- 90 RADIANS;
  every vlax-curve-* and ActiveX value derived from it is wrong;
- a drawing clautolisp writes stores radians where a vendor reads degrees
  (an ARC of 0..pi/2 opens in AutoCAD as 0..1.57 degrees).

Round trips clautolisp -> clautolisp are consistent, which is why no test
saw it.

* Reproduction

#+begin_src lisp
(with-input-from-string
    (s (format nil "0~%SECTION~%2~%ENTITIES~%0~%ARC~%5~%2A~%8~%0~%10~%0.0~%20~%0.0~%30~%0.0~%40~%10.0~%50~%0.0~%51~%90.0~%0~%ENDSEC~%0~%EOF~%"))
  (clautolisp.drawing:dxf-read-drawing-from-stream s))
;; entity data: ((5 . "2A") (0 . "ARC") (8 . "0") (10 0.0 0.0 0.0) (40 . 10.0)
;;               (50 . 0.0) (51 . 90.0))          <- entget would say 1.5708
#+end_src

* Cause

=dxf-parse-value= / =dxf-write-data-pair= treat every real group the same.
The degree-valued groups depend on the entity type (ELLIPSE 41/42 are
radians -- parameters, not angles; LWPOLYLINE 42 is a bulge), so the
conversion needs a per-type table.

* Proposal

A per-entity-type table of degree groups (from the DXF reference), applied
in =dxf-load-entities= / =dxf-load-blocks= (degrees -> radians) and in the
entity writer (radians -> degrees). Check the DWG codec (LibreDWG reports
radians) stays untouched. Tests: read a vendor-written DXF with an ARC, a
rotated TEXT and an INSERT; write and re-read; compare with a probe-captured
entget.

Found while fixing cador-curve-length-and-sampling (the vlax-curve-* model
used to convert ARC angles from degrees, which happened to match a
DXF-loaded drawing but not entmake / command / ActiveX).

* Fix (2026-10-22)

=clautolisp/drawing/source/dxf.lisp= gains a per-entity-type table of
degree-valued groups, =*dxf-degree-groups*=, taken from the DXF reference:

| type      | groups      | meaning                                          |
|-----------+-------------+--------------------------------------------------|
| ARC       | 50 51       | start / end angle                                |
| TEXT      | 50 51       | rotation / oblique angle                         |
| ATTRIB    | 50 51       | rotation / oblique angle                         |
| ATTDEF    | 50 51       | rotation / oblique angle                         |
| SHAPE     | 50 51       | rotation / oblique angle                         |
| MTEXT     | 50          | rotation (when written instead of the 11 vector) |
| INSERT    | 50          | rotation                                         |
| DIMENSION | 50 51 52 53 | rotation, horizontal dir, oblique, text rotation |
| VERTEX    | 50          | curve-fit tangent direction                      |

Deliberately absent: ELLIPSE 41/42 (parameters, radians in the file too)
and the LWPOLYLINE / VERTEX 42 bulge. Only the first occurrence of each code
is converted, and the scan stops at 75/76 (MTEXT column data, whose column
heights reuse 50), 101 (embedded object) and 1001 (XDATA).

=dxf-entity-from-file= (degrees -> radians) is applied in
=dxf-load-entities= and =dxf-load-blocks= (block-owned entities); the
writer's =dxf-entity-data-with-owner= (used for ENTITIES and BLOCKS) applies
=dxf-entity-for-file= (radians -> degrees) to a copy, so the in-memory data
is not mutated. ASCII and binary DXF share these paths. Table records, block
headers, OBJECTS and header variables are not converted.

The DWG codec (=drawing-dwg/source/codec.lisp=) is untouched: it converts
DWG <-> DXF through libredwg and parses / emits that DXF with this codec,
and libredwg's DXF is degree-valued like any vendor's, so DWG reads and
writes become correct through the same code. No other place compensated:
=autolisp-host/source/curve-geometry.lisp= already treats ARC 50/51 as
radians (the cador-curve-length-and-sampling fix), and the degree
conversions in cador (command-api, command-draw, command-hatch,
command-builtins, prompt-api) convert *command input* to radians, which is
correct.

Tests (=clautolisp/drawing/tests/dxf-tests.lisp=):
- =dxf-read-converts-file-degrees-to-radians= -- a literal DXF with an ARC
  0..90, a TEXT (rotation 45, oblique 15), an INSERT (rotation 30), an
  ELLIPSE (42 = pi, must stay pi) and a block-owned TEXT (rotation 180);
- =dxf-write-emits-degrees= -- an ARC 0..pi/2 is written as 0 and 90; an
  LWPOLYLINE bulge 42 is written unchanged;
- =dxf-angle-round-trip= -- write then read gives the entget angles back,
  and the source drawing is not mutated;
- =dxf-mtext-column-heights-are-not-angles=.

Red on the unfixed codec (=make test-sbcl
TEST_SYSTEM=clautolisp/drawing/tests=): 349 checks, 7 failures -- "ARC end
angle 90 deg must read as pi/2, got 90.0d0", "TEXT rotation 45 deg must read
as pi/4, got 45.0d0", "INSERT rotation 30 deg must read as pi/6, got
30.0d0", the TEXT oblique and the block-owned TEXT, "ARC 51 in the file must
be 90: 1.5707963267948966d0", and the MTEXT test (helper undefined). The
round-trip test passed there too, as the ticket predicted (clautolisp ->
clautolisp was self-consistent). Green with the fix: 350 checks, 0 failures.

Status NEXT, not DONE: the table comes from the DXF reference only; no
vendor-written DXF measured on AutoCAD / BricsCAD was available. Still to
confirm against one (entget of the same entities), in particular MTEXT 50
(the DXF reference text says "radians", while vendor files and ezdxf treat
it as degrees -- the table follows the latter) and DIMENSION 51/52. Not
covered, left for a follow-up if needed: HATCH 52/53 and its boundary-edge
arc angles, VIEWPORT 51, the VPORT / VIEW table records, header angle
variables -- see dxf-angle-units-hatch-viewport-tables.issue.

* Probe (2026-10-23)

Verification is now a CAD probe plus a fixture test (branch
probe-dxf-angles):

- =autolisp-front-end/tests/scenarios/entities/dxf-angles-probe.lsp=, run
  by =scripts/run-dxf-angles-probe.sh= / =.ps1=, family =dxf-angles= of
  =scripts/ci-detect-probe-changes.py=, jobs =dxf-angles:probe:bricscad:macos=,
  =...:bricscad:windows=, =...:autocad:windows=, =...:accoreconsole:windows=
  in =.gitlab/native.yml= (automatic when the probe changes, else manual;
  soft). On layer DXFANG it entmakes an ARC 30..120, a TEXT (rotation 45,
  oblique 15), an ATTDEF (30 / 10), two MTEXT rotated 60 (one by 50, one by
  the 11 direction), an INSERT rotated 30, an attributed INSERT (45) with
  its ATTRIB (45 / 15), a 2D POLYLINE whose VERTEX has a 30-degree
  curve-fit tangent; and a DIMENSION by command (DIMLINEAR text angle 20,
  Rotated 30, then DIMEDIT Oblique 15). It prints entget's angle groups
  (=DXFANG ENTGET=), exports the drawing as DXF (vla-SaveAs ac2018_dxf,
  else SAVEAS DXF / DXFOUT), reads the file back by handle and prints the
  same groups as written (=DXFANG FILE=). Report and DXF:
  =dist/dxf-angles/<backend>-<os>.txt= and =.dxf=.
- =dxf-vendor-fixtures-angle-units= (=clautolisp/drawing/tests/dxf-tests.lisp=)
  loads every =*.dxf= under =clautolisp/drawing/tests/fixtures/vendor-dxf/=
  and checks that each probe object's claimed groups load as the file's
  degrees * pi/180 AND equal the vendor's entget from the =<name>.txt=
  report beside it. Empty today (passes trivially); see the README.org
  there.

Close this ticket when a vendor pair (AutoCAD and BricsCAD) is in the
fixture directory and the test is green; MTEXT 50 and DIMENSION 51/52 are
the groups to read first in the reports. The clautolisp baseline run
(=--backend clautolisp=) shows file = entget * 180/pi for every entity
case; its DIMENSION case is FAILED (cador has no DIMLINEAR), and its DXF
header holds ISO-8859-1 bytes in an AC1027 file
(dxf-writer-header-not-utf8.issue).

* Measured on the CADs (2026-10-23, dxf-angles probe, MR !472) -- DONE, 2.3.43

DXFOUT (COM SaveAs) of entities with known angles, the file compared with
the CAD's own entget, on AutoCAD 2022 (job 17409369691), BricsCAD V25
Windows (17409369690) and V26 macOS (17409369689): degrees in the file,
radians in entget, for ARC 50/51, TEXT / ATTDEF / ATTRIB 50/51, INSERT 50,
VERTEX 50 and DIMENSION 50 / 53 (28 groups on AutoCAD, 26 on each
BricsCAD -- every pair). DIMENSION 51 / 52 at their default 0 are not
written.

Two codec defects the vendor files showed, fixed in 2.3.43:
- DIMENSION: the 75 / 76 stop meant for MTEXT's column section stopped the
  scan before a DIMENSION's 53 and 50 (its 75 comes first), so they loaded
  in degrees. The stop now applies to MTEXT only.
- MTEXT: the vendors write the rotation as the 11 / 21 direction only (no
  50) while their entget lists (50 . angle). The loader now derives 50 from
  11 when the file gives none, and the writer leaves 50 out when there is
  an 11.

The vendor DXFs and probe reports are fixtures now
(clautolisp/drawing/tests/fixtures/vendor-dxf/: AutoCAD 2022 Windows,
BricsCAD V26 macOS); DXF-VENDOR-FIXTURES-ANGLE-UNITS loads each with the
codec and checks every probe object against the file's degrees AND the
CAD's own entget: green (584 checks), red on 2.3.42's codec (DIMENSION and
MTEXT).
